#: ../../iam/password-management/samba-policies.rst:8
msgid "Samba domain password policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../iam/password-management/samba-policies.rst:10
msgid ""
"With the Samba domain object, you can set the requirements for user "
"account passwords in a Samba domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../iam/password-management/samba-policies.rst:13
msgid ""
"You can manage the Samba domain object through the *LDAP directory "
"module* in the *Management UI*. For more information, see :external+uv-"
"nubus-manual:ref:`nubus-domain-ldap` in :cite:t:`uv-nubus-manual`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../iam/password-management/samba-policies.rst:20
msgid ""
"Univention recommends configuring the Samba domain object's password "
"requirements to match the user password policy as described in :ref"
":`password-management-policies`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../iam/password-management/samba-policies.rst:24
msgid ""
"UDM policies apply when administrators change passwords through "
"administrative tools. Samba domain policies apply when users change their"
" own passwords through any service. Because these are separate systems, "
"Univention recommends configuring them identically to ensure consistent "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../iam/password-management/samba-policies.rst:36
msgid ""
"In the LDAP directory, navigate to the ``samba`` container underneath the"
" LDAP base DN and select the Samba object. The Samba object has the "
"domain's NetBIOS name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../iam/password-management/samba-policies.rst:41
msgid ""
